    <briefdescription>
<para>An overloaded function to assign a value to a field. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Allocate and initialize a new value and return the index. If an error condition occurs the parameter NO_FIELD is returned.</para><para>If the type of the field is changing (e.g. real values being transformed to integers), then any previous values for the field are removed and replaced by the value passed in the present call to this function.</para><para>If append is present and .true., then index cannot be greater than 0 if it is present. <linebreak/>
 Example usage: <programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="normal">field_index=<sp/><ref refid="interfacefield__manager__mod_1_1fm__new__value" kindref="compound">fm_new_value</ref>(name,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">value</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[create],<sp/>[index],<sp/>[append])</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
